any structure step ƛ that is ※ during that scene.
Some scenes will have these structure tags, but many will not.
KEY POINT: Be prepared to change your scene ô when you start writing individual
scenes.
When it comes to actually writing a scene, you may find that the basic action خring in that scene
is not what you thought. You will only know that for sure when you get "inside" the scene and write it. So
be flexible. What's important at this point in the process is to get an overview of what you think the single
main action of each scene will be.
Be aware that the average م movie has forty to ʟ scenes. A Ñ ordinarily has twice
